# Lab 20: Companion registration delete experiment
#
# Question:
# After an approved disposable GCP source agent is deleted and Registry Sync
# confirms its absence, can the mapped companion Registration, companion
# Package, dedicated Agent Identity, Blueprint, and Blueprint principal be
# retired safely while a durable mapping records every partial state?
#
# Run one request at a time. Never use "Send All".
#
# Parts 1 and 2 are read-only. Parts 3 through 5 contain separately gated
# destructive actions. Registration deletion is irreversible through the
# tested API. Agent Identity and Blueprint deletion are soft deletion; they
# are not permanent purge.
#
# Put all real values in the shared ignored ../../.env file:
#
# A365_TENANT_ID=<directory-tenant-id>
# A365_CLIENT_ID=<public-client-application-id>
# A365_DEMO_ORIGINAL_PACKAGE_ID=<registry-sync-package-id>
# A365_DEMO_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID=<exact-provider-source-agent-id>
# A365_DEMO_ASSIGNMENT_MODE=<dedicated-or-shared>
# A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_GROUP=<mapped-assignment-group>
# A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_OBJECT_ID=<mapped-blueprint-object-id>
# A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID=<mapped-blueprint-app-id>
# A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_PRINCIPAL_ID=<mapped-blueprint-principal-id>
# A365_DEMO_AGENT_IDENTITY_ID=<dedicated-agent-identity-id>
# A365_DEMO_COMPANION_SOURCE_AGENT_ID=<exact-mapped-companion-source-id>
# A365_DEMO_COMPANION_REGISTRATION_ID=<companion-registration-id>
# A365_DEMO_COMPANION_REGISTRATION_ID_PATH=<path-safe-registration-id>
#
# Save private responses only under:
# ../../evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/
#
# Read proposal.md before running this experiment. After completing it, compare
# the run with findings.md. The mapping helper is local-only and does not call
# Microsoft Graph or a provider API.
#
# This file never deletes a shared Blueprint or the Registry Sync connection.
# Dedicated Blueprint cleanup is an optional, separately approved experiment.

@tenantId = {{$dotenv A365_TENANT_ID}}
@clientId = {{$dotenv A365_CLIENT_ID}}
@originalPackageId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_ORIGINAL_PACKAGE_ID}}
@expectedSourceAgentId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID}}
@assignmentMode = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_ASSIGNMENT_MODE}}
@blueprintGroup = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_GROUP}}
@blueprintObjectId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_OBJECT_ID}}
@blueprintAppId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID}}
@blueprintPrincipalId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_PRINCIPAL_ID}}
@agentIdentityId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_AGENT_IDENTITY_ID}}
@companionSourceAgentId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_COMPANION_SOURCE_AGENT_ID}}
@companionRegistrationId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_COMPANION_REGISTRATION_ID}}
@companionRegistrationIdPath = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_COMPANION_REGISTRATION_ID_PATH}}
@graphBaseUrl = https://graph.microsoft.com
@deleteScopes = https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FUser.Read%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FCopilotPackages.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FApplication.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentityBlueprint.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentity.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentity.DeleteRestore.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentRegistration.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentRegistration.ReadWrite.All%20offline_access
@blueprintDeleteScopes = https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentityBlueprint.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentityBlueprint.DeleteRestore.All%20offline_access

###############################################################################
# Mapping initialization - run once before Part 1
#
# Run from the Lab 20 directory:
#
# python demos/03-delete-companion/prototype_retirement_mapping.py `
#   --mapping evidence/demos/02-rename-companion/mapping-after-rename.json `
#   --output evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/mapping.json `
#   initialize
#
# The helper replaces the old ambiguous top-level status with lifecycleStatus,
# adds lifecycleReason, and adds retirement plus blueprintCleanup state. It
# preserves all IDs, relationships, names, and assignment metadata. Do not
# initialize the same output twice.

###############################################################################
# Authentication 1 - Request a device code
#
# Never save this response.

# @name deleteStartDeviceCode
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/devicecode
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id={{clientId}}&scope={{deleteScopes}}

###

###############################################################################
# Authentication 2 - Exchange the device code after browser sign-in
#
# Never save this response.

# @name deleteToken
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Agrant-type%3Adevice_code&client_id={{clientId}}&device_code={{deleteStartDeviceCode.response.body.$.device_code}}

###

###############################################################################
# Part 1.1 - Confirm the signed-in operator
#
# Send after Authentication 2 succeeds. Expected: 200.

# @name deleteCurrentUser
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/me?$select=id
Authorization: Bearer {{deleteToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 1.1
#
# Do not save this response. The operator ID is used only by the live session.

###############################################################################
# Part 1.2 - Capture complete Package inventory before provider deletion
#
# Expected: 200. Read every returned page and locate the original Package using
# its exact scoped provider source key, not display name alone.

# @name deleteListPackagesBefore
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{deleteToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 1.2
#
# 1. Save the first page:
# ../../evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/package-list-before-provider-deletion-page-1.json
# 2. If @odata.nextLink exists, save every additional page as
#    package-list-before-provider-deletion-page-2.json, page-3.json, and so on.
# 3. Confirm there is exactly one provider Package and one companion Package
#    for the mapping before continuing.

###############################################################################
# Part 1.3 - Capture the original Registry Sync Package
#
# Expected: 200. Confirm its nested provider sourceAgentId equals the exact
# value saved in A365_DEMO_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID.

# @name deleteGetOriginalPackageBefore
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{originalPackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{deleteToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 1.3
#
# Save:
# ../../evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/provider-package-before-deletion.json

###############################################################################
# Part 1.4 - Verify the mapped Blueprint
#
# Expected: 200. Confirm its object ID and appId match the locked assignment.

# @name deleteGetBlueprintBefore
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/applications/{{blueprintObjectId}}/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprint
Authorization: Bearer {{deleteToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 1.4
#
# Save:
# ../../evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/blueprint-before-deletion.json

###############################################################################
# Part 1.5 - Verify the enabled Blueprint principal
#
# Expected: 200. Confirm id equals A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_PRINCIPAL_ID, appId
# equals A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID, and accountEnabled is not false.

# @name deleteGetBlueprintPrincipalBefore
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals(appId='{{blueprintAppId}}')/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal
Authorization: Bearer {{deleteToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 1.5
#
# Save:
# ../../evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/blueprint-principal-before-deletion.json

###############################################################################
# Part 1.6 - Capture the mapped companion Registration
#
# Expected: 200.
# Confirm:
# - ID equals A365_DEMO_COMPANION_REGISTRATION_ID
# - sourceAgentId equals A365_DEMO_COMPANION_SOURCE_AGENT_ID exactly
# - do not delete solely to replace a valid legacy source namespace
# - Blueprint and Agent Identity links match the durable mapping

# @name deleteGetRegistrationBefore
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/beta/copilot/agentRegistrations/{{companionRegistrationIdPath}}
Authorization: Bearer {{deleteToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json
OData-Version: 4.0

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 1.6
#
# Save:
# ../../evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/companion-registration-before-deletion.json

###############################################################################
# Part 1.7 - Capture the mapped Agent Identity
#
# Expected: 200. Confirm the ID and Blueprint appId match the mapping.

# @name deleteGetIdentityBefore
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals/{{agentIdentityId}}/microsoft.graph.agentIdentity
Authorization: Bearer {{deleteToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 1.7
#
# Save:
# ../../evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/agent-identity-before-deletion.json

###############################################################################
# Part 1.8 - OPTIONAL inspect direct app-role assignments
#
# An Agent Identity is a service principal. It can be granted application
# permissions to Microsoft Graph, another Microsoft API, or a customer API
# independently of its companion Registration. Deleting the Registration does
# not prove that these grants are unused. Deleting the Agent Identity removes
# the service principal that holds them and can break a separate runtime,
# scheduled job, or integration that still authenticates as this identity.
#
# This request lists app-role assignments granted directly to the mapped Agent
# Identity. The response normally identifies the target resource service
# principal and app role by IDs. Resolve or classify those IDs only through an
# already approved directory read; do not copy real IDs into tracked files.
#
# Example A - empty value array:
# No direct app-role assignment was observed. This reduces one deletion risk,
# but it does not prove that the Identity is unused. Runtime bindings, OAuth
# grants, directory roles, group-derived access, policies, owners, and external
# provider credentials are outside this one response.
#
# Example B - expected disposable permission:
# The Lab may have granted this Identity an application role on Microsoft Graph
# or a test API. Confirm that the grant belongs only to this disposable demo,
# that no remaining runtime uses it, and that retirement approval covers losing
# that access. Do not remove the assignment merely to make this check empty.
#
# Example C - unexpected enterprise permission:
# The response might resolve to a role such as a mail, files, SharePoint, or
# customer-API application permission that was not part of the Lab. Treat that
# as evidence of another consumer or an unresolved dependency. Stop deletion
# and ask the permission owner to identify its purpose.
#
# A non-empty result does not automatically block retirement forever, and an
# empty result does not automatically approve retirement. The result supplies
# evidence for the dependency review at Stop A and Stop B.
#
# This documented service-principal relationship requires the separately
# consented Application.Read.All permission. Do not request broader permission
# solely to make this experiment pass. If this read is not already approved,
# classify dependency inspection as unavailable and stop before deletion.
#
# Expected when approved: 200. A non-empty response requires dependency
# review; it is not authorization to remove assignments or delete the identity.

# @name deleteGetIdentityAppRoleAssignments
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals/{{agentIdentityId}}/appRoleAssignments
Authorization: Bearer {{deleteToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 1.8 WHEN THE READ IS APPROVED
#
# Save:
# ../../evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/agent-identity-app-role-assignments-before-deletion.json
#
# If the read is unavailable, do not fabricate an empty result. Record the
# boundary outside response evidence and stop before destructive steps.

###############################################################################
# Part 1.9 - Inspect direct directory memberships
#
# An Agent Identity can be placed in a directory group independently of its
# companion Registration and direct app-role assignments. A group can be used
# to grant access, select identities for governance, organize an approved agent
# population, or drive customer automation. Deleting the Agent Identity removes
# the directory object that participates in those relationships and can change
# behavior outside this Lab.
#
# This request reads the mapped Agent Identity's direct memberOf relationships.
# It answers "which directory containers directly include this Identity?" It
# does not enumerate every transitive group, every policy that references a
# group, or every external system that copied the membership.
#
# Example A - empty value array:
# No direct directory membership was observed. This removes one dependency
# concern, but it does not prove that the Identity is unused. Part 1.8,
# runtime-binding review, policy review, and external-system checks remain
# separate.
#
# Example B - expected disposable Lab group:
# The Identity might belong to a temporary group used only to identify Demo 1
# objects or grant disposable test access. Confirm the group is truly
# experiment-only and that no remaining object or automation expects this
# member before approving deletion.
#
# Example C - unexpected business or production group:
# The Identity might appear in a group such as "Approved Production Agents",
# "Finance Automation", or a group that has access to a customer API. That can
# mean another workflow deliberately adopted this Identity after creation.
# Stop deletion and ask the group owner what access, policy, reporting, or
# automation depends on the membership.
#
# Example D - unfamiliar directory object type:
# memberOf can return directory objects that are not understood from their
# display name alone. Do not guess from the name or remove the relationship.
# Classify it as an unresolved dependency until an approved directory owner
# identifies the object and its purpose.
#
# A non-empty result requires dependency review; it is not permission to remove
# the Identity from a group. An empty result is not retirement approval. The
# result contributes evidence to Stop A and Stop B together with the direct
# app-role assignment check.
#
# Expected: 200. Preserve the private response locally. Put only safe counts
# and classifications such as empty, expected-lab-only, or unresolved in
# tracked findings.

# @name deleteGetIdentityMemberships
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals/{{agentIdentityId}}/microsoft.graph.agentIdentity/memberOf?$select=id,displayName
Authorization: Bearer {{deleteToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 1.9
#
# Save:
# ../../evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/agent-identity-memberships-before-deletion.json

###############################################################################
# Manual provider checkpoint - no request
#
# Only with explicit approval, delete the existing disposable GCP source agent
# through its supported provider interface.
#
# Record private provider evidence, then wait for:
# - a successful Registry Sync cycle;
# - the agreed propagation/grace period; and
# - a healthy connection with no permission or connector errors.
#
# Provider deletion alone does not authorize companion cleanup. Continue with
# the read-only Registry Sync observations below.

###############################################################################
# Part 2.1 - Read complete Package inventory after provider deletion and sync
#
# Expected: 200. Read every page.
#
# Search by the exact scoped provider source key:
# - If the same key has a new Package ID, update the mapping and STOP.
# - If the original Package or another matching source remains, STOP.
# - If inventory is partial or the connector is unhealthy, STOP.

# @name deleteListPackagesAfterSourceDeletion
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{deleteToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 2.1
#
# Save the first page immediately:
# ../../evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/package-list-after-provider-deletion-page-1.json
#
# If @odata.nextLink exists, save every additional page as
# package-list-after-provider-deletion-page-2.json, page-3.json, and so on.
# Do not send Part 2.2 until every page is saved.

###############################################################################
# Part 2.2 - Probe the previous Package ID
#
# Possible results:
#
# - 200: the Package Details endpoint still resolves the old Package. Stop.
# - 404: the endpoint reports that the old Package is absent.
# - 424 Failed Dependency with UnknownError and the nested message
#   "Could not find Title Preview for given title.": classify the Package
#   Details probe as inconclusive-dependency-failure.
# - any other error: save it and stop for classification.
#
# The observed Title Preview 424 means the Package Details backend could not
# materialize a dependency for this ID. It is compatible with a disappearing
# Package, but it must not be treated as source-deletion proof or rewritten as
# a 404. Part 2.1 complete inventory, healthy sync, the grace period, and
# provider evidence remain the deletion evidence.

# @name deleteGetOriginalPackageAfter
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{originalPackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{deleteToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 2.2
#
# Save the previous Package ID response immediately, including a JSON error
# response:
# ../../evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/provider-package-after-deletion.json
#
# Then compare this response with every saved Part 2.1 page and search for the
# exact scoped provider source key.
#
# If the same source appears under a replacement Package ID, run:
#
# python demos/03-delete-companion/prototype_retirement_mapping.py `
#   --mapping evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/mapping.json `
#   --output evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/mapping.json `
#   event source-relocated --package-id "<replacement-package-id>"
#
# Confirm lifecycleStatus returned to active, then STOP. Do not delete any
# companion object.
#
# If the source key and previous Package ID are absent from every complete
# Part 2.1 inventory page, run the following for either:
#
# - a 404 Package Details response; or
# - the verified-target Title Preview 424 described above.
#
# The source-missing event records the complete-inventory observation. It does
# not convert the Package Details response into successful absence proof.
#
# Run:
#
# python demos/03-delete-companion/prototype_retirement_mapping.py `
#   --mapping evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/mapping.json `
#   --output evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/mapping.json `
#   event source-missing `
#   --grace-period-ends-at "<approved-ISO-8601-deadline>"
#
# Replace the angle-bracket placeholder with a real timestamp that includes a
# timezone. Do not run the command with the placeholder text. If no waiting
# policy is approved yet, omit --grace-period-ends-at and remain pending.
#
# This records:
# - lifecycleStatus=pending;
# - lifecycleReason=awaiting-grace-period;
# - providerSource.reason=provider-presence-unconfirmed; and
# - registrySyncPackage.reason=not-observed-in-complete-inventory.
#
# The grace-period reason belongs to the overall workflow because the system
# started the timer. It does not claim that the provider confirmed deletion.
# Re-run source-missing after later observations if the source remains absent;
# this advances lastCheckedAt without changing statusChangedAt or clearing an
# existing grace-period deadline.

###############################################################################
# CURRENT CHECKPOINT - STOP HERE until gracePeriodEndsAt
#
# Immediately after source-missing, confirm only:
# - lifecycleStatus is pending;
# - lifecycleReason is awaiting-grace-period;
# - providerSource is pending with reason provider-presence-unconfirmed;
# - registrySyncPackage is pending with reason
#   not-observed-in-complete-inventory;
# - companionRegistration, companionPackage, and agentIdentity remain active;
# - sourceRetirementApprovedAt is null; and
# - no DELETE request is authorized.
#
# Do not expect providerSource or registrySyncPackage to be retired yet.

###############################################################################
# Simulation-only grace policy - optional local mapping change
#
# The production candidate remains 14 days. To complete this disposable
# lifecycle experiment today without pretending that 14 days passed, an
# explicitly approved simulation may use a real 15-minute interval that has
# already elapsed since missingSince.
#
# Do not edit mapping.json manually and do not provide a future --at value.
# Run:
#
# python demos/03-delete-companion/prototype_retirement_mapping.py `
#   --mapping evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/mapping.json `
#   --output evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/mapping.json `
#   event configure-simulation-grace `
#   --simulation-grace-minutes 15 `
#   --production-candidate-grace-period P14D `
#   --reason validate-disposable-delete-lifecycle
#
# Confirm:
# - retirementPolicy.mode is experiment-simulation;
# - retirementPolicy.gracePeriod is PT15M;
# - retirementPolicy.productionCandidateGracePeriod is P14D; and
# - gracePeriodEndsAt equals missingSince plus 15 real minutes.
#
# This simulation validates lifecycle mechanics only. It does not validate
# that 15 minutes or 14 days is the correct production waiting policy.

###############################################################################
# Part 2.3 - Re-read complete inventory at the grace-period boundary
#
# Run this after the real grace deadline or after the approved simulation
# policy above. Expected: 200. Read and save every page before continuing.

# @name deleteListPackagesAtGraceEnd
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{deleteToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 2.3
#
# Save the first page:
# ../../evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/package-list-at-grace-end-page-1.json
#
# Save every @odata.nextLink page as page-2.json, page-3.json, and so on.
# Search all pages for the exact scoped provider source key and old Package ID.

###############################################################################
# Part 2.4 - Re-probe the previous Package ID at the grace boundary
#
# Expected: 404 or the already classified Title Preview 424. A 200 means the
# Package resolves again and retirement must stop.

# @name deleteGetOriginalPackageAtGraceEnd
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{originalPackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{deleteToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 2.4
#
# Save:
# ../../evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/provider-package-at-grace-end.json
#
# If the stable source appears under any Package ID, run source-relocated and
# STOP. Do not retire the source.
#
# If complete healthy inventory still contains no matching source or old
# Package ID, and Part 2.4 returned either 404 or the classified Title Preview
# 424, run source-missing again without changing the deadline:
#
# Run from the Lab 20 directory. If the command reports Preparation failed,
# do not continue; correct the working directory or path and rerun it.
#
# python demos/03-delete-companion/prototype_retirement_mapping.py `
#   --mapping evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/mapping.json `
#   --output evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/mapping.json `
#   event source-missing
#
# Require the command to print lifecycleStatus=pending, then reopen mapping.json
# and confirm lifecycleReason=awaiting-source-retirement-approval. Also confirm
# providerSource.lastCheckedAt is later than retirementPolicy.configuredAt.
# This second source-missing event records a real grace-end observation; it
# does not copy or reuse the earlier Package evidence.

###############################################################################
# Stop A - approve source retirement after the grace period
#
# Continue only when all conditions are true:
# - the current time is at or after gracePeriodEndsAt;
# - a new successful, healthy Registry Sync observation still finds the scoped
#   source key absent from every Package List page;
# - no replacement Package exists for the same source key;
# - the mapping still identifies exactly one companion Registration and Agent
#   Identity for that source;
# - no other active mapping references either object;
# - runtime use, grants, policies, memberships, owners, and other dependencies
#   have been reviewed; and
# - the approved sustained-absence policy authorizes source retirement.
#
# Provider confirmation is useful when an approved provider integration or
# human checkpoint supplies it, but automatic Registry Sync reconciliation
# cannot claim provider deletion. Without provider confirmation, retirement is
# based on the approved sustained-absence policy.
#
# Otherwise leave lifecycleStatus pending, or run block-object with an exact
# reason when a required safety check cannot be completed:
#
# python demos/03-delete-companion/prototype_retirement_mapping.py `
#   --mapping evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/mapping.json `
#   --output evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/mapping.json `
#   event block-object --object companionRegistration `
#   --reason "<safe-blocking-reason>"
#
# When all Stop A conditions are satisfied, run:
#
# python demos/03-delete-companion/prototype_retirement_mapping.py `
#   --mapping evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/mapping.json `
#   --output evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/mapping.json `
#   event source-retirement-approved
#
# The helper rejects this event before gracePeriodEndsAt. Its default provider
# reason is retired-by-sustained-registry-absence-policy. If separate provider
# evidence exists, supply a more specific approved --reason without changing
# the Registry Sync evidence classification.
#
# Confirm:
# - lifecycleStatus is pending;
# - lifecycleReason is companion-retirement-pending;
# - providerSource and registrySyncPackage are retired; and
# - companionRegistration is pending with reason approval-required.
#
# This event approves source retirement only. It does not approve or perform
# companion Registration deletion.

###############################################################################
# Stop A2 - separately approve companion Registration retirement
#
# Do not continue merely because companionRegistration is approval-required.
# That reason means the workflow is waiting for a separate decision.
#
# Continue only when:
# - Stop A retired providerSource and registrySyncPackage;
# - companionRegistration is pending with reason approval-required;
# - the Registration and Agent Identity IDs still match the dependency review;
# - no active mapping, runtime, grant, policy, membership, owner workflow, or
#   other reviewed dependency requires the Registration; and
# - explicit approval to delete this disposable companion Registration has
#   been obtained.
#
# After approval, record it before sending DELETE:
#
# python demos/03-delete-companion/prototype_retirement_mapping.py `
#   --mapping evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/mapping.json `
#   --output evidence/demos/03-delete-companion/mapping.json `
#   event registration-retirement-approved
#
# Confirm:
# - companionRegistrationRetirementApprovedAt is populated;
# - companionRegistration remains pending; and
# - companionRegistration.reason is retirement-approved.

###############################################################################
